[2026-11-27T11:42:15Z] note: assumptions: SPY is loaded as a signal-only reference series (never traded). | point-in-time universe: a member joins once it is listed and its indicators exist; before that it is not part of the ranking (same as breadth_scaled_sector_allocation). EXECUTION.md's 'skip the rebalance if a member lacks history' would otherwise move the start to the youngest ETF's listing (XLC 2018, DBC 2006). | cash earns 0 %: EXECUTION.md allows this only as the labelled conservative scenario; none of these rules needs a cash yield (no excess-cash momentum), so ^IRX isn't used. | costs: library convention (ETFs fee 0.05 % + slippage 0.03 % per fill; crypto 0.10 % + 0.10 %), same as the other library runs, so leaderboard entries compare. | Yahoo adjusted closes (dividends reinvested) serve as both the signal (total-return) and the fill series, like every other library run; EXECUTION.md's separate raw execution series isn't available. | participation cap (1 % of volume) not modelled: a 10k sleeve in liquid ETFs/coins never reaches it. | every month-end decision restores the target weights, trimming drift too; trims keep the holding's cost basis, stop and age, and don't close a trade (a trade = first buy to full exit).
